course: dictionary
lesson: 15852
title: Unevenness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unevenness is a noun. It is the state of being uneven, which means not flat, not smooth and not level. Think of the bumps on a road or the lumps in a bumpy carpet. Both have unevenness.
explain: «The unevenness of the old road made the bike bounce.» The road is not flat, so the bike bumps up and down. The word unevenness names this bumpy quality of the road.
explain: Unevenness also means not equal or not regular. «The unevenness of the sharing made Sam cross.» Sam was cross because the shares were not the same size. Uneven is the adjective you use to describe something, and unevenness is the noun that names the quality.
fact: Unevenness is the state of not being flat, smooth or level.
fact: Unevenness is also the state of not being equal or regular.
fact: «The unevenness of the old road made the bike bounce.» means the road had bumps and was not level.
fact: «The unevenness of the sharing made Sam cross.» means the shares were not equal.
fact: Uneven is the adjective, and unevenness is the noun. Unevenness is an uncountable noun, so you do not say "an unevenness" or "unevennesses".
exercise: «The unevenness of the old road made the bike bounce.» What does unevenness mean here? | Being flat and smooth | Being very quick | Having a bright colour | *Bumps, so the road is not level
exercise: «The unevenness of the sharing made Sam cross.» What was uneven? | The sharing was done quickly | *The shares were not equal | Sam shared nothing at all | Sam was happy with the sharing
exercise: Which word names the state of not being level? | flat | level | *unevenness | smooth
test: What does unevenness mean in fairness talk? | Being quiet and calm | Being very large | *Not being equal or fair in shares | Being exactly equal
test: Which is the best example of unevenness in a surface? | A still pond | *A bumpy path with loose stones | A flat sheet of paper | A smooth glass table
exam: Why did the ball roll unevenly across the field? | It was night-time and the ball could not be seen | The ball was too heavy to roll | *The unevenness of the bumpy ground made the ball change direction | The field was perfectly smooth
